{
  "summary": "The RNA-only, multiprofile scVI_n200 configuration with avgpool achieved validation accuracy 0.6501 and F1 0.6275, higher than the prior single-profile scVI_n200 result of 0.5203 accuracy and 0.4982 F1, as well as the earlier RNA PCA and image-only baselines. This suggests that adding multiprofile aggregation to the strongest RNA representation may provide a substantial validation improvement over the single-profile baseline, though the comparison does not isolate the effect of multiprofile modeling from avgpool aggregation. It remains uncertain whether this result reflects a general benefit of multiprofile modeling, a specific benefit of avgpool, or uncontrolled factors in the scVI_n200 pipeline."
}

